Crossbill is an independent iPhone wallet. It is not affiliated with, endorsed by or supported by the Shrike
or Sparrow projects, Bitcoin Knots, Lightning Fork, Paperclip or Connor's Lab. Before version 0.4.0 it was called "Shrike for
iPhone".

Parts of it are reimplemented, in TypeScript and Swift, from Shrike (https://github.com/privkeyio/shrike,
https://shrikewallet.com), an unofficial fork of Sparrow Wallet (https://github.com/sparrowwallet/sparrow) that
follows the BLAKE2b proof-of-work fork. Shrike and Sparrow are licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0.

These parts are ported from Shrike and its drongo library (https://github.com/privkeyio/drongo) and were
rewritten in TypeScript for this app, which changes them from the originals:

  src/core/replay.ts     the replay protection decision (AppServices.chainDecision and heightDecision)
  src/core/sighash.ts    the unified opt-in signature hash
  src/core/sign.ts       signing rules, including drongo's low-R signature grinding
  src/core/txbuilder.ts  coin selection and change, modeled on Sparrow's
  src/core/sync.ts       compatibility with Sparrow's Cormorant watch-only wallet on Bitcoin Core/Knots
  src/core/explorer.ts   block explorer links, as Shrike builds them

Lightning: Crossbill talks to the mobile API of the Lightning Fork dashboard, the web interface that Paul Lamb
forked from Umbrel's Lightning app for Lightning Fork (https://github.com/paulscode/lightning-fork), his LND
fork for the BLAKE2b chain. Crossbill's client (src/core/lfapi.ts) is written from that API's documentation,
docs/mobile-api.md in https://github.com/paulscode/umbrel-lightning-fork. No code from the dashboard, from
Lightning Fork or from its Android app is included. tools/lf-mock is a pretend dashboard written for Crossbill's
tests from the same documentation.

The Crossbill Wallet logo, a red low-poly crossbill in front of a shield, is Crossbill's own, as are the app
icon, launch image and in-app images made from it (resources/icon.png, public/bird.png, and the Splash and
Bird image sets).

Some names inside the code still say "shrike": the Keychain service, the storage folder, the backup file's
format tag, the skin IDs, the widget kinds and the native plugin. They are kept so that phones and backups from
earlier versions keep working, and none of them are shown in the app. They are not a use of the Shrike name as
this product's brand.

